   Route::get('/protected-route', function () {
       // ... route logic
   })->middleware('ip_whitelist');
   ```

   Or apply it to a group of routes:

   ```php
   Route::middleware(['ip_whitelist'])->group(function () {
       Route::get('/route1', ...);
       Route::post('/route2', ...);
   });
   ```


**Important Security Note:**  Relying solely on IP whitelisting for security is generally *not recommended*. IP addresses can be spoofed.  It's best to use IP whitelisting as an *additional* security layer combined with stronger authentication methods.

