1. **Get Command-Line Arguments:**
   - `env::args()` returns an iterator over the command-line arguments.
   - `.collect()` converts the iterator into a `Vec<String>`.  `args[0]` is the program name itself, `args[1]` will be our substring, and `args[2]` will be the string to search within.

