Since your code only lists the formatting of variables `Treatment`, `Effectiveness`, and `Sex`, and doesn't explicitly mention any other variables, the simplest solution is to just list the variables you *want* to keep:

```sas
data vertical3;
	set vertical2;
	keep Treatment Effectiveness Sex;  /* List variables to keep */
format Treatment $Drug. Effectiveness $Effective. Sex $Sex. ;
run;
```

By using the `KEEP` statement, you specify exactly which variables should be included in the `vertical3` dataset. Any variables not listed in the `KEEP` statement (including the unnamed "column A" if it exists) will be excluded.


Alternatively, if you know the name of "column A", you can use a `DROP` statement:

```sas
data vertical3;
